  m_text: 'A composite value type is one value made of several values. A Vector3 holds three floats: x, y and z. A Color holds four floats: r, g, b and a (red, green, blue, alpha). new Vector3(2f, 0.5f, 1f) makes one Vector3 out of three numbers.


    <b>Predict:</b> How many fields does the Inspector show for size, and what is in each of them?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Select Box 2. Find Composite Types in the Inspector.

    2. Click the Tint box: the color picker shows its four values.

    3. Look at Position in the Transform: it is a Vector3 too.'
